{
  "_about": "Dictionary IPA (ipa-dict) differs from the phoneme symbols a TTS model was trained on. Each set says how to recognise such a model (its symbol table or its config's phoneme_type), which languages it applies to (empty = all), and the rewrites applied in order to every dictionary pronunciation. stress_before_vowel moves a stress mark from the start of the syllable to its vowel, as espeak-ng and misaki write it. missing_symbol_fallback rewrites a symbol only for a model whose symbol table lacks it (e.g. Kokoro has no ɦ or dental mark, nor the Polish/Serbian ʐ ʑ or the German ʏ, said with the nearest symbol it has). Chao tone letters (˥˥ ˧˥ ˨˩˦ ˥˩) become tone arrows for a model without them.",
  "vowels": "aeiouyæɐɑɒɔəɘɚɛɜɞɤɨɪɯɵɶʉʊʌʏøœAIOQWY",
